      "writtenOn": "2024-07-26T23:33:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could make it a little more robust by nuking any non-alphanumerics:\n\n`std::replace_if(name.begin(), name.end(), [](char c) { return !isalnum(c); }, \u0027_\u0027);`\n \nFWIW, by the letter of the law, we don\u0027t have to do anything--the OpName in SPIR-V is basically just a comment. (However, there are known cases where SPIR-V compilers will misbehave if two things are given overlapping names, so it\u0027s better to be safe here!)",
